  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "reveal": "Left subtree, then the node, then the right subtree. On a binary search tree that comes out in sorted order."
 },
 "takeaway": "Traversal is recursion: handle left, the node, and right in some order. Inorder on a BST gives sorted values.",
 "code": [
  "void inorder(Node n) {",
  "  if (n == null) return;",
  "  inorder(n.left);",
  "  visit(n);",
  "  inorder(n.right);",
  "}"
